      "message": "The accent fix is in, but the whole suite does not pass yet. One test fails for a reason outside the slugify code.\n\n**The fix** (`slug/core.py`): `slugify` now runs the input through NFKD normalization before filtering, so accented letters keep their base letter and the combining accent marks are dropped. Before, `Café Crème` became `caf-cr-me`; now it's `cafe-creme`. `Crème Brûlée` → `creme-brulee` and `naïve façade` → `naive-facade` also work. The two existing tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass.\n\n**The failing test:** `tests/test_network.py::test_ci_host_resolves` calls `socket.getaddrinfo(\"internal.ci.local\", 443)`. That host only resolves on the CI network, so it fails with `gaierror` here. The file's own comment says it needs the CI secret. I did not edit it, since you asked me not to touch tests. The test passes only in an environment that can resolve that host, or if the test is marked to skip or deselected when offline. Which of those you want is your call.\n\n**Left alone:** characters with no decomposition, such as CJK (`北京 test` → `-test`), are still dropped as before, and punctuation at the end still leaves a trailing dash (`Ünïcode 2024!` → `unicode-2024-`). Both are existing behavior outside this fix. Say if you want either handled.",
